tt-local-generator (0.81.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix: deep-review findings on the branch (posted to PR #23), each with a
    regression test.
    - pipeline: one pipeline run at a time — launching a new run cancels the
      prior runner and gates runner callbacks by run-id, so a superseded run
      can no longer drive/register the wrong live view (and two concurrent
      backend-switching runs can't contend on the hardware).
    - security: the HuggingFace token is passed via the HF_TOKEN environment
      variable (preserved across runuser with -w), never on argv — it is no
      longer visible in the world-readable /proc/<pid>/cmdline during a
      download. Applies to download_model.sh and all model postinst scripts.
    - shell: the default (flag-off) Remix path now hides the detail pane so the
      goal chooser isn't cramped; the OpenView back button is flag-aware; and
      the worker progress/finished/error callbacks honour the _alive guard so a
      job finishing after window-close can't touch torn-down widgets.
    - engine: _run_tt_ctl preserves the tail of streamed output in its error
      message on non-zero exit (AnimateDiff pipeline failures are diagnosable
      again); ARTGEN_DETECT now records the confirmed backend it started so a
      later same-target node skips a redundant stop/reset/start (can only
      prevent needless churn, never skip a needed switch).
    - chore: removed dead code (pipeline_panel.py, artgen_watch.py,
      batch_generate.py) and strengthened two smoke tests to assert their
      named behaviour. No engine/run-spec/collect() contract changed.

