tt-local-generator (0.68.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * feat(create): "👁 Watch" viz now drives the memory layer from per-chip POWER
    draw, not AICLK. Investigation of "the viz barely responds during
    AnimateDiff" found AICLK on Blackhole is effectively binary (~800 idle /
    1350 boosted) and often sits pinned at 1350 even at rest, so it barely moved
    during a job. Power draw is graded and tracks real utilisation (~18 W idle ->
    150 W+ under diffusion), so each chip's memory layer now pulses with its own
    real load and the header reads live watts. Read via a lightweight background
    tt-smi poll (~0.3 s snapshot, 1.5 s cadence, off the GTK thread) since the
    fast pyluwen lib is venv-only and the app runs system python; falls back to
    sysfs AICLK when tt-smi is unavailable. New pure helpers parse_powers/
    power_intensity/sample_telemetry (unit-tested).

